<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caucasus Line Cossack Host</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1832">1832</a>–<a href="/years/1860">1860</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> Line <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> Host was formed in 1832 from Cossack regiments settled along the fortified Caucasus Line on the Terek and Kuban rivers. It garrisoned the frontier during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasian-war">Caucasian War</a> against the mountain peoples. In 1860 it was divided: its western regiments merged with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> Cossack Host to form the Kuban Cossack Host, and the rest became the Terek Cossack Host.</p></div>
